        "original_id": "599b7fc4-51d6-5d77-8ff4-3fad82efa0c0",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Sir John Wedderburn, 5th Baronet of Blackness; Charles Edward Stuart; Henry Benedict Stuart; James Francis Edward Stuart\n- Events: Jacobite uprising of 1745; Battle of Culloden\n- Topics: Jacobitism; treason\n\nFacts:\n- In 1745, Charles Edward Stuart instigated the unsuccessful Jacobite uprising and led an insurrection to restore his family to the throne of Great Britain.\n- Sir John Wedderburn, 5th Baronet of Blackness, was a Perthshire gentleman who joined Charles Edward Stuart's 1745 rebellion.\n- Sir John Wedderburn, 5th Baronet of Blackness, was captured at the Battle of Culloden and afterwards convicted of treason.\n- Henry Benedict Stuart, unlike his father James Francis Edward Stuart and his brother Charles Edward Stuart, made no effort to seize the throne.",
